  "formulas": {
    "score": "s=dot(Q_r,K_origin)/sqrt(2)",
    "causal_mask": "masked iff key_position > query_position",
    "maximum": "m_new=max(m_old,s) for an unmasked block",
    "old_scale": "a=0 if m_old is -infinity; otherwise exp(m_old-m_new)",
    "new_scale": "b=exp(s-m_new)",
    "denominator": "l_new=a*l_old+b",
    "numerator": "u_new=a*u_old+b*V_origin",
    "output": "O=u/l when l>0; otherwise null (undefined)",
    "masked_block": "skip the entire block; keep m,l,u,O unchanged; do not evaluate -infinity - (-infinity)"
  },
  "scope": [
    "Arithmetic teaching example: three ranks, one local query token and one KV token per rank, one attention head, d_k=d_v=2. It is not a GPU benchmark or a claim about a specific framework implementation.",
    "Each rank keeps its own Q and online m/l/u/O state. Only KV blocks move clockwise r -> (r+1)%3. An incoming KV block is identified by its original token position.",
    "Round0 uses local KV. After two exchanges, all ranks have computed three origin blocks exactly once. There is no extra exchange after round2.",
    "Full attention has no causal mask. Causal attention allows key_position <= query_position using global token positions, not rank arrival order.",
    "m is the running maximum over visible scores; l is the max-shifted exponential sum; u is the max-shifted weighted value sum. O is a normalized partial result until every required block has been processed.",
    "A masked score is stored as its finite raw value plus masked=true; it contributes neither probability nor numerator. null m represents -infinity only for the empty initial state, and null O represents no visible key yet.",
    "Numerical states are saved at full Python float precision; the renderer may round to four decimal places. Sources for the surrounding explanation are maintained by the parent page."
  ],
